  "id": "cyclopean-eye",
  "term": "cyclopean eye",
  "definition": "The cyclopean eye is an imagined single eye located in the middle of the forehead, used to describe how we mentally locate objects in space. It refers to the fact that visual directions are treated as if they came from one central eye rather than from two separate eyes.",
